---
term: Delegation
section: execution
order: 20
definition: A grant of authority from one body to another to act on its behalf within defined limits.
seeAlso:
  - delegated-public-authority
  - delegation-of-functions
---
A corporation can delegate upward to a parent, for example by giving territorial authority to a regional corporation. It can also delegate outward to an [[executive agent]]. Delegation transfers the power to act. It doesn't transfer the power to redefine the interest being served. Central banking calls this split *instrument independence* without *goal independence* (Debelle and Fischer, 1994). The government sets the inflation target, and the central bank chooses how to reach it.

The Social Charter aims to combine decentralized information and representation with centralized or highly delegated execution. Once members legitimately set an objective, they can delegate its implementation deeply.
